%I A400221 #10 Sep 27 2026 04:35:51
%S A400221 1,48,297,1024,2625,5616,10633,18432,29889,46000,67881,96768,134017,
%T A400221 181104,239625,311296,397953,501552,624169,768000,935361,1128688,
%U A400221 1350537,1603584,1890625,2214576,2578473,2985472,3438849,3942000,4498441,5111808,5785857,6524464,7331625,8211456,9168193,10206192
%N A400221 Number of divisors of 3360^n.
%C A400221 3360 = 2^5*3*5*7 is the least integer whose prime exponents are 5, 1, 1, 1, so a(n) = (5*n+1)*(n+1)^3, and a(n) is equally the number of divisors of (p^5*q*r*s)^n for any distinct primes p, q, r, s.
%C A400221 a(n) is the number of filled cells of the 4-dimensional generalized Menger sponge with subdivision 2n+1: number the coordinates of a (2n+1)^4 grid from 0 and keep the cells with at most one odd coordinate; a(1) = 48 is the first iteration of the 4-dimensional Menger sponge.
%C A400221 The same rule in dimension D keeps (n+1)^(D-1)*((D+1)*n+1) cells: A005408 (D = 1), A000567 (D = 2), A103532 (D = 3, the divisors of 240^n), this sequence (D = 4); the column n = 1 is A001792.
%C A400221 The kept cells are the (n+1)^4 cells with every coordinate even plus the 4*n*(n+1)^3 cells with exactly one odd coordinate; the shared factor (n+1)^3 is why the count is a divisor function.
%H A400221 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400221/b400221.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400221 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (5,-10,10,-5,1).
%F A400221 a(n) = (n+1)^3*(5*n+1).
%F A400221 a(n) = A000005(3360^n).
%F A400221 a(n) = (n+1)^4 + 4*n*(n+1)^3.
%F A400221 G.f.: (1 + 43*x + 67*x^2 + 9*x^3)/(1 - x)^5.
%F A400221 a(n) = 5*a(n-1) - 10*a(n-2) + 10*a(n-3) - 5*a(n-4) + a(n-5) for n > 4.
%e A400221 a(1) = 48: 3360 = 2^5*3*5*7 has 6*2*2*2 = 48 divisors, and the 3 X 3 X 3 X 3 grid has 16 cells with every coordinate even and 4*8 = 32 cells with exactly one odd coordinate.
%t A400221 A400221[n_] := (n + 1)^3*(5*n + 1); Array[A400221, 50, 0] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 27 2026 *)
%o A400221 (Python)
%o A400221 print([(n+1)**3*(5*n+1) for n in range(38)])
%Y A400221 Cf. A000005 (number of divisors), A000567 (dimension 2), A000583 (the all-even cells), A001792 (column n = 1), A005408 (dimension 1), A016756 (the full grid), A103532 (dimension 3).
